Snippet 1
Time complexity: O(n)
Space complexity: O(1)
Justify: Checks each item in the array once from start to finish while keeping track of only one maximum value.

Snippet 2
Time complexity: O(n^2)
Space complexity: O(1)
Justify: Uses two loops to compare every single element against every other element, using no extra storage.

Snippet 3
Time complexity: O(log n) 
Space complexity: O(log n) 
Justify: Chops off one digit at a time by dividing by 10, leaving a small stack of waiting recursive calls in memory.

Snippet 4
Time complexity: O(n^2)
Space complexity: O(n^2)
Justify: Combines every item with every item to create pairs, saving all n^2 combinations in a list.

Snippet 5
Time complexity: O(log n)
Space complexity: O(1)
Justify: Cuts the remaining search space in half each step without saving any extra data structures.

Snippet 6
Time complexity: O(n^3)
Space complexity: O(n^2)
Justify: Uses three nested loops to multiply two grids, building a new n x n matrix to store results.

Snippet 7
Time complexity: O(m * n)
Space complexity: O(k)
Justify: Scans every single box in a grid, but only stores memory for the k non-zero values it finds.

Snippet 8
Time complexity: O(n^2)
Space complexity: O(1)
Justify: The double loop takes much longer than the single loop, so it determines the total runtime.

Snippet 9
Time complexity: O(n)
Space complexity: O(1)
Justify: The inner loop runs a fixed 10 times for each item, so total work scales directly with n.

Snippet 10
Time complexity: O(n)
Space complexity: O(n)
Justify: Loops through the original list backwards once and creates a brand-new list of the same size.

Snippet 11
Time complexity: O(n)
Space complexity: O(1)
Justify: Swaps elements in place moving inward from both ends, requiring zero extra list memory.

Snippet 12
Time complexity: O(n)
Space complexity: O(n)
Justify: Calls itself n times recursively, holding n unfinished function calls stacked in memory.

Snippet 13
Time complexity: O(2^n)
Space complexity: O(n)
Justify: Branches into two new recursive calls at every step, creating a growing tree of calls up to depth n.

Snippet 14
Time complexity: O(n)
Space complexity: O(n)
Justify: Scans the list once using a quick lookup set that stores up to n unique numbers.

Snippet 15
Time complexity: O(n * 2^n)
Space complexity: O(n)
Justify: Generates all 2^n subsets and loops n times for each subset to extract its items.

Snippet 16
Time complexity: O(n + m)
Space complexity: O(n + m)
Justify: Steps through two sorted lists once side-by-side, placing all items into a new combined output list.

Snippet 17
Time complexity: O(n)
Space complexity: O(n)
Justify: Makes a full reversed copy of the string in memory before checking if it matches the original.

Snippet 18
Time complexity: O(m * n)
Space complexity: O(m * n)
Justify: Visits every box in an m x n grid and copies each value into a single flat list.

Snippet 19
Time complexity: O(exp)
Space complexity: O(exp)
Justify: Subtracts 1 from the exponent each step, holding a stack of recursive calls equal to the exponent size.

Snippet 20
Time complexity: O(log(exp))
Space complexity: O(log(exp))
Justify: Halves the exponent at every recursive step, keeping call depth and total operations very small.

Snippet 21
Time complexity: O(|a| * |b|)
Space complexity: O(1)
Justify: Compares every item in list a against every item in list b using no additional memory.

Snippet 22
Time complexity: O(n)
Space complexity: O(u) (or O(n) where u is unique elements)
Justify: Reads the list once and builds a dictionary storing counts for each unique element u.